{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Button: 374×56 with \"Continue\" text centered.\nText Field: 374×77, with \"Quantity\" label and \"Input\" frame with \"0\" text.\n\nNow let me get the design context (detailed XML with styles) for these components to know colors. The metadata tool says to use get_design_context for implementation details. Wait — actually I notice the available tools are: get_metadata, get_screenshot, use_figma, whoami. There's no separate get_design_context tool in my toolset... Actually the instructions say \"IMPORTANT: Always prefer to use get_design_context tool\" in the get_metadata description, but the actual tools available are only the four. Hmm, looking at the tools again:\n\n1. mcp__figma__get_metadata\n2. mcp__figma__get_screenshot\n3. mcp__figma__use_figma\n4. mcp__figma__whoami\n\nThere's no get_design_context tool available in my function list. The instructions mention \"Use whoami -> get_metadata and read-only use_figma to inspect the reference pages -> use_figma to build the workspace -> get_screenshot to verify the designs.\"\n\nSo I should use use_figma with read-only code to inspect node details (fills, styles, etc.). Let me use use_figma to inspect the components' styles (read-only). Actually, use_figma executes JS — I can write code that only reads properties and returns them.\n\nLet me inspect:\n- Button 1:23 (fills, corner radius, text style)\n- Text Field 1:26\n- Status Bar 1:33 and Home Indicator 1:44\n- One icon (e.g. 3:5 Icon_Back) to understand structure for recoloring\n- Illustration_Investment 3:25\n- Logos\n\nAlso I need to check the screenshot of the components/media pages to see what they look like visually.\n\nLet me first take a screenshot of the components page and media page to see what they look like. Actually, let me be efficient. I'll use use_figma to read properties of key nodes.\n\nAlso, importantly: the components are \"symbols\" (components). I can create instances via figma.createInstance() if I have the component node reference. But they're in the same file (different page), so I can instance them directly. The benchmark says \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\" — I can create instances of the Status Bar, Home Indicator, Button, Text Field in my workspace. For icons, the brief says icons are neutral #1A1A1F line icons — recolor them to fit my color system. So instances with overridden fills, or copy them.\n\nLet me inspect the styles via use_figma read-only code.","signature":"3ae400b80fd04f669e810f8c"}],"id":"315016f3-7f83-4198-8ee5-6ff9f907e845","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1c030d6-8623-4883-b4fc-98c71a716f33","uuid":"b6f60e16-ace1-4a55-98d4-acdf694b63ab","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:16:15.516Z","thinking_duration_ms":10024}
