tton: #12B76A? Hmm wait — on 05, \"Buy\" with Icon_Arrow_Up and \"Sell\" with Icon_Arrow_Down are actions. Buy → green #12B76A, Sell → #FA5555? But Sell is entry-only (no link). Buy on 05 goes to 06. Actually wait: on 05 the links are \"Buy → 06_Stock_Transaction → back → 04_Portfolio\". The \"Buy\" there is the Buy action. And 06's \"Buy\" button goes to 07. On 07, \"Cancel\" and \"Buy\" (Buy is entry-only on 07).\n\nLet me use a consistent primary CTA = brand red #FA5555 for the main \"Buy\" actions (per the given Button component which is red). Then Buy/Sell toggle on 05: Buy = red (brand, primary), Sell = secondary surface. That keeps the given red Button as THE primary CTA and matches the prototype links (Buy is the linked action). Good — this avoids green/red CTA confusion and uses the provided Button component directly. Gains/change values still green +brand-red as data colors.\n\nHmm, but classic trading UX has green Buy. The brief says buy/sell colors are mine. I'll do: Buy = brand red primary (uses given Button), Sell = outlined/secondary neutral. Clean, coherent, and uses the fixed component.\n\n**Type scale (Inter):**\n- Large title: 32/38 Bold (Home greeting/balance)\n- Title 1: 24/30 Bold (screen headers \"Investment Portfolio\")\n- Title 2: 20/26 Bold\n- Headline: 17/22 Semi Bold\n- Body: 16/22 Regular (button text 16 Semi Bold given)\n- Subhead: 14/18 Medium/Semi Bold (labels)\n- Caption: 12/16 Regular\n- Micro: 10/12 (tab labels, caps)\n\n**Spacing:** 4-base grid; screen margin 24; card padding 16-20; section gap 24-32.\n\n**Radii:** buttons 16 (given), cards 16-20, inputs 12 (given), chips 8-12, dialog 24.\n\n**Elevation:** subtle shadows on cards (light screens only), dark screens use surface contrast.\n\n**Layout per frame (414×896):**\n\n**01_Home (light):**\n- Status bar (black glyphs)\n- Header: greeting? The must-include says balance $3,821 (Icon_Safe), Vulcan Bank payment card (no number), 2 pages dots current 1, actions: My card (Icon_Card)