eft-aligned title next to back reads better. Title at x=76 y center 18 SB. Right icons: at x from right: insights at 414-24-24=366; chart at 366-24-20=322; menu at 322-24-20=278. For Transaction: menu only at 366. Dot on chart (Portfolio only): red 8px at chart icon top-right.\n\nHmm, title \"Investment Portfolio\" 18 SB ≈ 165px. 76+165=241 < 278. OK.\n\nHeader variants: Portfolio / Trading / Transaction — same structure, chart dot visibility differs (Portfolio: visible; Trading: hidden; Transaction: no chart/insights icons → set visible=false).\n\nComponent set \"VI/Header\": 3 variants named Style=Portfolio etc.\n\n**QuickAction**: 96×76: circle 56 (white fill, shadow light) icon centered recolored dark #1A1A1F, label below 12 SB dark. Text override per instance (\"My card\" etc.) + icon instance swapped? Swapping icon inside instance: instance.children — replace icon instance with another? For master QuickAction, master contains Icon_Card instance. Per-screen instances need different icons: I can swap by deleting icon child in the instance and inserting new icon instance? Editing instance children structure (add/remove) is NOT allowed on instances (structure is locked; only certain overrides). Overriding via `instance.setProperties` only for variants. Icon swap trick: make the inner icon a nested COMPONENT SET? Alternative: QuickAction master WITHOUT icon; screens place icon instance + QuickAction? Ugly.\n\nBetter: make QuickAction a component set with variants per icon? 3 variants (Card/Transfer/Mobile) + label override. That works: combineAsVariants 3 masters \"Icon=Card|Transfer|Mobile\".\n\nSame issue HistoryRow icons (Location/Transfer/Transfer_In) → variants Icon=Location|Transfer|TransferIn (3 masters). And CaseRow logos (Apple/Tesla/Netflix/Microsoft) → variants Logo=Apple|Tesla|Netflix|Microsoft (4 masters). StockHeader logo Apple only — single component w/ Logo_Apple instance.\n\nTabBar: same 5 icons, but which is active differs per screen — variants Active=Main|Invest (2 masters, light/dark too): Theme=Light,Active=Main / Theme=Dark,Active=Invest. 2 masters.\n\nHeader: 3 variants (Style=Portfolio|Trading|Transaction) — inner icons same, just visibility overrides per variant master. Fine.\n\nKeypadKey: single master w/ text overrides (digit + letters). Letters text override per instance. Backspace key: not a KeypadKey variant — I'll place icon directly.\n\nPinCell: variants State=Filled|Empty (digit text override on Filled).\n\nPeriodChip: variants State=Active|Default (label override).\n\nAccountOption: variants State=Selected|Default (code/balance override).\n\nButtonSecondary: variants Theme=Light|Dark (label override). Sell/Cancel use Dark.\n\nStat: single master (label/value override). Used in 05 twice. 04 summary custom inline.\n\nDialog: single master \"VI/Dialog\" containing title + Cancel/Buy buttons? Cancel = ButtonSecondary instance, Buy = Button instance (given). Dialog master 320×~180. Place instance in 07.\n\nTotal masters: 2 (tabbar) + 3 (header) + 3 (quickaction) + 3 (historyrow) + 4 (caserow) + 1 (stockheader) + 1 (stat) + 2 (periodchip) + 1 (keypadkey) + 2 (pincell) + 2 (accountoption) + 2 (buttonsecondary) + 1 (dialog) = 27 nodes → 11 sets/components. \n\nScreenshot check flow at end.\n\nAlso don't forget: 01 must ALSO have status bar (black) + home indicator (black). 02/03 same light. 04-07 white glyphs.\n\nEdge: recoloring StatusBar instance: children text \"9:41\", Signal frame (children vectors w/ fills?), Wifi ellipse fill, Battery frame stroke (+ maybe fill child). I'll recolor fills+strokes to white except name 'Notch'.\n\nLet me now write Call 1: helpers + TabBar set + Header set.\n\nKey APIs:\n- figma.createComponent(); comp.resizeWithoutConstraints(w,h)\n- comp.appendChild(node)\n- figma.createInstance(); inst = iconComp.createInstance()\n- figma.combineAsVariants([c1,c2], parentPage)\n- setProperties on instances of sets: inst.setProperties({'Theme':'Dark','Active':'Invest'})\n- Text: const t = figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'Inter',style:'Semi Bold'}; t.characters='...'; t.fontSize=16; t.fills=[solid]\n\nLoad fonts first: await Promise.all([...['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:s}))])\n\nGradient fills: type 'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientTransform [[cos,-sin,tx],[sin,cos,ty]]... For horizontal L→R: [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]]. Vertical top→bottom: [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]]. I'll use those known matrices.\n\nShadow: effects [{type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x,y}, radius, spread?, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}]\n\nLet me write the code now. I'll aim for correctness and moderate length. Also remember every component master should live on page 5:2 (workspace), positioned in a \"components zone\" above the frames (y 0..1000), frames start y≈1400.\n\nComponent zone layout: rows of masters with labels? Skip labels, arrange neatly: x across.\n\nActually — for eval \"component reuse\", masters just need to exist & be used. I'll lay them in a grid: components section header text \"VI · Components\" at (0,0), masters grid starting y=80: each row height ~120, x spacing 440.\n\nCall 1 code:\n\n```js\nconst page = figma.getNodeById('5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfor (const s of ['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','Bold']) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter', style:s});\n\nconst C = {\n  accent:{r:0.980,g:0.333,b:0.333},\n  white:{r:1,g:1,b:1},\n  textDark:{r:0.102,g:0.102,b:0.122},   // #1A1A1F\n  secLight:{r:0.541,g:0.541,b:0.580},   // #8A8A94\n  secDark:{r:0.604,g:0.604,b:0.651},    // #9A9AA6\n  bgLight:{r:0.965,g:0.965,b:0.980},    // #F6F6FA\n  surface:{r:1,g:1,b:1},\n  bgDark:{r:0.055,g:0.059,b:0.078},     // #0E0F14\n  surfaceDark:{r:0.090,g:0.094,b:0.122},// #17181F\n  surfaceDark2:{r:0.122,g:0.129,b:0.165},// #1F212A\n  dividerDark:{r:0.149,g:0.157,b:0.200},// #262833\n  dividerLight:{r:0.918,g:0.918,b:0.941},// #EAEAF0\n  gainLight:{r:0.071,g:0.651,b:0.420},  // #12A66B\n  gainDark:{r:0.184,g:0.839,b:0.576},   // #2FD693\n};\nconst solid = (c, o=1) => [{type:'SOLID', color:c, opacity:o}];\n...\n```\n\nrecolor helper:\n```js\nfunction recolor(n, col, skip=[]) {\n  if (skip.includes(n.name)) { /* still recurse? no */ }\n  else {\n    if ('fills' in n && Array.isArray(n.fills)) {\n      if (n.fills.length) n.fills = n.fills.map(f => f.type==='SOLID' ? Object.assign({}, f, {color:col}) : f);\n    }\n    if ('strokes' in n && Array.isArray(n.strokes) && n.strokes.length) n.strokes = n.strokes.map(s => s.type==='SOLID' ? Object.assign({}, s, {color:col}) : s);\n  }\n  if ('children' in n) n.children.forEach(c => recolor(c, col, skip));\n}\n```\nCareful: Object.assign on paint objects ok.\n\nIcons registry:\n```js\nconst ICON = {};\nfor (const [k,id] of Object.entries({ArrowDown:'3:2',ArrowRight:'3:6',ArrowUp:'3:4',Back:'3:5',Backspace:'3:3',Card:'3:7',Cashback:'3:8',Chart:'3:9',ChevronRight:'3:10',Insights:'3:11',Invest:'3:12',Location:'3:13',Main:'3:14',Menu:'3:15',Mobile:'3:16',More:'3:17',Payment:'3:18',Payments:'3:19',Plus:'3:20',Safe:'3:21',Search:'3:22',Transfer:'3:23',TransferIn:'3:24'})) ICON[k]=figma.getNodeById(id);\nconst LOGO = {Apple:figma.getNodeById('3:26'),Microsoft:figma.getNodeById('3:27'),Netflix:figma.getNodeById('3:28'),Tesla:figma.getNodeById('3:29')};\nconst SHELL = {status:figma.getNodeById('1:33'),home:figma.getNodeById('1:44')};\nconst BTN = figma.getNodeById('1:23'); // Button\nconst TF = figma.getNodeById('1:26');  // Text Field\n```\n\nmkText:\n```js\nfunction mkText(chars, size, style, col, ls=0) {\n  const t = figma.createText();\n  t.fontName = {family:'Inter', style};\n  t.fontSize = size;\n  t.characters = chars;\n  t.fills = solid(col);\n  if (ls) t.letterSpacing = {unit:'PIXELS', value:ls};\n  return t;\n}\n```\nNote: must set fontName before characters (after loading font). ok.\n\nTabBar master builder(theme, active):\n```js\nfunction buildTabBar(theme, active) {\n  const comp = figma.createComponent();\n  comp.name = ...; comp.resizeWithoutConstraints(414,80);\n  const dark = theme==='Dark';\n  comp.fills = solid(dark?C.bgDark:C.bgLight);\n  // hairline\n  const line = figma.createRectangle(); line.resize(414,1); line.fills = solid(dark?C.dividerDark:C.dividerLight); comp.appendChild(line); line.x=0; line.y=0; line.name='Divider';\n  const tabs = [['Main','Main'],['Payments','Payments'],['Cashback','Cashback'],['Invest','Invest'],['More','More']];\n  const col = dark?C.white:C.textDark;\n  const inact = C.secDark; // same both\n  const actCol = C.accent;\n  tabs.forEach(([label,icon],i)=>{\n    const x = 24 + i*73.2 + ... // 5 tabs across 366: each slot 73.2\n    const isActive = label===active;\n    const ic = ICON[icon].createInstance(); ic.x = ...center\n    recolor(ic, isActive?actCol:inact);\n    comp.appendChild(ic);\n    const lb = mkText(label, 10, 'Medium', isActive?actCol:inact);\n    ...\n  });\n}\n```\nPositions: slot width 366/5 = 73.2, start x=24. Icon centered in slot: x = 24 + i*73.2 + (73.2-24)/2. Label centered: set textAlignHorizontal center w/ autoresize? Text autoResize default WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT; center by x = slotCenter - t.width/2.\n\nCombine variants: c1.name='Theme=Light, Active=Main'; c2.name='Theme=Dark, Active=Invest'; const set = figma.combineAsVariants([c1,c2], page); set.name='VI/Tab Bar'; position set at x,y. Note: after combine, set.resize? The set bounds auto. Position set x=0 y=80.\n\nWait — does combineAsVariants move components into a set on the page? Yes: combineAsVariants(nodes, parent, index).\n\nHeader builder(style):\n```js\nfunction buildHeader(style) {\n  const comp = figma.createComponent(); comp.name='Style='+style; comp.resizeWithoutConstraints(414,44); comp.fills=[];\n  const back = ICON.Back.createInstance(); recolor(back, C.white); back.x=24; back.y=10; comp.appendChild(back);\n  const title = mkText(TITLES[style], 18, 'Semi Bold', C.white); title.x=76; title.y=11; comp.appendChild(title);\n  const iconsRight = style==='Transaction' ? ['Menu'] : ['Menu','Chart','Insights'];\n```\nWait brief order: \"menu (Icon_Menu) · chart (Icon_Chart, with an unread dot) · insights (Icon_Insights)\" — display order: menu, chart, insights (left→right). Place: insights rightmost at x=414-24-24=366; chart at 366-24-18=324; menu at 324-24-18=282. For Transaction: menu at 366.\nDot: ellipse 8 at chart.x+24-6? top-right: x=chart.x+20,y=6? Icon_Chart is 29×26 — instance w 29. dot at x+w-5, y=2.\n\nBut visibility per variant: for Portfolio dot visible; Trading hidden. Since each variant is its own master, just don't add dot for Trading; for Transaction only menu.\n\nTitles: Portfolio: \"Investment Portfolio\"; Trading: \"Trading\"; Transaction: \"Stock transaction\".\n\nAll headers dark (only used on dark screens). Name variants 'Style=Portfolio' etc. Set name 'VI/Header'.\n\nCall 1 returns IDs of sets. Then Call 2: small components:\n- QuickAction set (Icon=Card|Transfer|Mobile): comp 96×84: circle 56×56 radius 28 white + shadow(light), icon centered dark; label 12 SB dark centered below at y=64.\n- HistoryRow set (Icon=Location|Transfer|TransferIn): comp 366×64: avatar 44 rounded 14 white w/ icon dark 24 centered; title 16 SB dark x=60 y=10; sub 13 R secLight x=60 y=34; amount 16 SB right-aligned x to 366 (set x = 366 - width). amount color override per instance (dark or gain). Name text overrides: instance.findChild... I'll name layers: 'Title','Sub','Amount','Avatar','Icon'.\n- CaseRow set (Logo=Apple|Tesla|Netflix|Microsoft): comp 366×56: logo 40×40 (instance scaled? Logo components are 48×48; instance.resize(40,40) scales children? For components with vector children, resizing instance scales proportionally? Instance resize scales the instance box; vector children with constraints SCALE will scale. Constraints of logo children: probably default MIN/MIN — resizing might not scale vectors. Safer: keep logo 48×48 or use rescale? I'll use inst.rescale(40/48)? There's node.rescale(scale) — yes,