ox w=110 h=13 y=42 CENTER (letterSpacing 1). Digits 1-9,0: '1' has no letters? Standard: 1 blank, 2 ABC, 3 DEF, 4 GHI, 5 JKL, 6 MNO, 7 PQRS, 8 TUV, 9 WXYZ, 0 (blank or +?). Brief: keypad 1-9/0 with letters (2 ABC…9 WXYZ). So 1 and 0 letters empty. Override letters to '' for those.\n\nPinCell Filled: digit fixed box w=56 h=30, y=(64-30)/2=17, CENTER. Override chars 9/7/7.\n\nAccountOption SymbolText: fixed box w=36 h=20, x=0, y=8, CENTER. Override '$'/'€'. Code 'USD'/'EUR' left-aligned auto OK. Sub balances left OK.\n\nDialog Title: fixed box w=320 h=25, x=0, y=28, CENTER. Keep 'Are you sure?'.\n\nQuickAction label: fixed w=110 h=15, x=0, y=66, CENTER. Override 'My card'/'Transfer'/'Mobile' — variants already distinct so no override needed.\n\nChip Label: fixed w=64 h=16, x=0, y=10, CENTER. Override Week/Month/Year/All on instances.\n\nButton Secondary/Compact label: fixed w=137 h=20, x=0, y=16, CENTER.\n\nGiven Button label override: characters + textAutoResize='NONE' + align CENTER, keep box (71×19). 'Start' 'Ready' 'Buy' fit. \n\nWait — does setting textAutoResize='NONE' on that text change its size? It keeps current box (71×19). align CENTER centers 'Start' in 71-wide box at x151.5 → centered in 374 button. \n\nAlso — the 'VI/Stat' has Label/Value left auto-resize — fine.\n\nAlso the recolor for Status Bar on dark screens: skip 'Notch'.\n\nNow write the corrected full component build. Also delete nothing (previous call fully rolled back — inventory showed only Tab Bar/Header/labels exist).\n\nOne more check — combineAsVariants requires components not attached to page? They were appended to page via x/y assignment... In previous successful Tab Bar build I used same pattern. combineAsVariants(nodes, page) — nodes must not be children of another component? They're top-level on page (created via figma.createComponent() which attaches to currentPage). But I set comp.x/comp.y AFTER creation — fine. Note: buildQuickAction doesn't set comp.x/y — defaults 0,0; combineAsVariants handles positioning into the set frame. Then I set set position. Fine.\n\nAlso variant property naming: comp.name='Icon=Card' etc. Good.\n\nAlso: after combineAsVariants, the set is a ComponentSetNode — resize? The set auto-sizes. Positioning set.x/y fine.\n\nAlso for PinCell Empty variant — dashes: dashPattern [5,5] — I set strokeWeight 1.5 gray #B5B5BF (0.71). On light bg OK.\n\nHeight/size checks:\n- QuickAction 110×84: circle 56 + label y66 h15 = 81 < 84 OK.\n- HistoryRow 366×64: avatar y10 h44 = 54, title y11, sub y35 h16=51 OK.\n- CaseRow 366×64: logo 48×48 at y8 → 56 OK.\n- StockHeader 366×52: price y2 h25=27, change y32 h16=48 OK. Logo 48 at y2 → 50 OK.\n- Chip 64×36: label h16 y10 → 26 OK.\n- KeypadKey 110×64: digit y8 h28=36, letters y42 h13=55 OK.\n- PinCell 56×64: digit h30 y17 → 47 OK.\n- AccountOption 366×60: symbol y12 h36=48, code y12, sub y34 h16=50 OK. Radio y20 h20=40 OK.\n- Button Secondary 137×52: label y16 h20=36 OK.\n- Dialog 320×196: title y28 h25=53, buttons y112 h52=164 OK.\n\nNow — will `recolor` on icon instance change the Avatar? recolor(ic) only touches ic subtree. Icon components are #1A1A1F vectors → recolor to textDark. OK.\n\nNote: ICON recolor for HistoryRow 'TransferIn' icon → textDark. OK.\n\nAlso for CaseRow logos: logos keep brand colors — NO recolor. OK.\n\nLet me also plan Stat: two instances on 05 (Market Value $97.83; Buying Power $18,943.43).\n\nNow write the call. Also guard: after building everything, return ids. Keep under 50k chars — fine.\n\nAlso important: NO t.y in setBtnLabel. But wait — the given Button text box: after setting characters to 'Start', textAutoResize stays WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT? I set textAutoResize='NONE' explicitly → keeps 71×19. align CENTER. Good.\n\nAlso the Dialog: b2Set.children[0] is Theme=Dark variant (first). createInstance, resize(137,52) — instance resize allowed. Text box inside is w137 fixed → centers. Cancel chars already 'Cancel'. Buy = Button Compact new master.\n\nOrder: build Button Secondary set BEFORE Dialog (need children). And Button Compact before Dialog. OK.\n\nEdge: `figma.combineAsVariants` with variants of different fill setups — fine.\n\nWrite it.","signature":"4fdaad5b88f74897b8406568"}],"id":"c614ce1a-0349-4b83-b59a-186d355d5f44","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1c030d6-8623-4883-b4fc-98c71a716f33","uuid":"2e78fbca-9c6d-4f3d-9def-d83ad778dfa8","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:35:35.591Z","thinking_duration_ms":146255}
