ild screens.\n\nActually, to save calls, I'll inspect them in the same call as building screen 01? No — need names BEFORE overriding. Since variants are used as-is (no child overrides needed for tab bar/header), I don't need names. Titles: if Header includes title text, great; if not, I add title separately on the frame. To be safe, inspect both sets' structure in a quick dump combined with the screen-01 build? If header lacks title, my screens would miss titles — screenshot would reveal.\n\nBetter: quick dump of 7:62 and 7:116 children (one call), then build. Let me do it.","signature":"5470a46372ea4af3adf3c009"}],"id":"0f2a83cb-8f68-4ee5-aeb9-a280af1a8a2f","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1c030d6-8623-4883-b4fc-98c71a716f33","uuid":"b39903e0-f29a-4fd6-902f-897410b87072","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:38:28.008Z","thinking_duration_ms":25874}
