{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Line 27: `f.appendChild(figma.getNodeById('1:33').createInstance()).y=0;` — appendChild returned null?? No — appendChild returns the node. Hmm, \"cannot set property 'y' of null\" — so appendChild returned null or getNodeById('1:33') returned null... createInstance of null would throw differently (\"cannot read property of null\"). Actually `figma.getNodeById('1:33').createInstance()` — if null → \"cannot read property 'createInstance' of null\". The error is setting .y of null — so appendChild(...) returned null. \n\nInteresting: appendChild returns the child normally. But maybe in this environment appendChild returns undefined/null?? Earlier calls (component build) did `comp.appendChild(circ); circ.x=27;` — separate statements, no return use. And Tab Bar build earlier presumably similar. So appendChild may return null in this environment!\n\nWait, actually — in Figma plugin API appendChild returns void? No — in the real API, appendChild returns void (undefined)! Actually checking: FrameNode.appendChild(child: BaseNode): boolean? Hmm, real signature: appendChild returns void. Yes — in the official Figma plugin API, appendChild returns nothing (void). So `.y` on undefined → error. My bad.\n\nFix: separate statements. Everything else in the call used separate statements already. Just line 27. Rewrite call with fix.","signature":"0b8a54771c0d48b8a320c1e3"}],"id":"63a0e1ae-5926-43df-b20a-1e4edd13be91","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1c030d6-8623-4883-b4fc-98c71a716f33","uuid":"ae995547-8ee3-4d57-b80e-d61e15bf9772","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:40:09.495Z","thinking_duration_ms":6632}
