{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"05 done (18:440). Now 06_Stock_Transaction + 07_Confirm_Purchase with shared builder.\n\n06 layout (x=494, y=2516):\n- status bar white, header Transaction\n- 'ACCOUNT' 12 Medium secDark ls1 at (24,116)\n- Account options at (24,140) Selected USD; (24,208) Default EUR\n- Text Fields: y=300 (Quantity), y=393 (Price). Use instance resize to 366: set Input constraints STRETCH first? Instance child constraints: try setting; if throws, fallback native 374 at x=20. I'll implement with try/catch: attempt inst.resize(366,77) after setting Input constraints; catch → keep 374 at x=20.\n  Actually simpler and safe: keep native 374 width at x=20 for both fields. Mixing 366/374 barely noticeable. But right caption inside input: place at x=20+374-17-w. Fine, skip constraints risk.\n  Fields at x=20: label at (20+0...) — the field instance has internal label at x0. Field1 (20,300): Label 'Quantity' fill secDark; Input fill surfaceDark2 stroke dividerDark; value '1' fill white. Caption '1 lot = 1 stock' at right inside input: input abs x=20, y=300+25=325, h=52 → caption y=342; x=20+374-17-w.\n  Field2 (20,393): Label 'Price'; value '$143.43'; caption '1 unit = $143.43' inside right.\n- info row y=486: 'commission $14.34' secDark 13 at x=20? left; maybe right side? Put left at 20+17? Align with input padding x=37. \n- Buy: given Button at (20,706) label 'Buy', name 'BtnBuy'.\n- Tab bar Dark Invest (0,782), home indicator white.\n\n07 (x=988, y=2516): same content build + Buy button too, then Dim rect (0,0,414,896, black 0.55) and Dialog instance at (47,330). Dialog on top. Home indicator white.\n\nShared function buildTx(f) does everything except Buy/tabbar/home? Include buy+tab+home in shared too (07 has them under dim — realistic).\n\nCode:\n\nfunction buildTx(f){\n  status bar, header Transaction\n  ACCOUNT label\n  account options x2 with overrides\n  text fields x2 with overrides + captions\n  commission row\n  Buy button (name BtnBuy)\n  tabbar, home indicator\n}\n\nFor account overrides: SymbolText '$'/'€', Code 'USD'/'EUR', Sub '$18,943.43'/'€16,473.11'.\n\nText Field overrides: \nconst tf=figma.getNodeById('1:26').createInstance(); f.appendChild(tf); tf.x=20; tf.y=Y;\nconst lbl=tf.findOne(n=>n.name==='Quantity'&&n.type==='TEXT'); lbl.characters=labelName; lbl.fills=solid(C.secDark);\nconst input=tf.findOne(n=>n.name==='Input'); input.fills=solid(C.surfaceDark2); input.strokes=solid(C.dividerDark); input.strokeWeight=1;\nconst val=input.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'); val.characters=value; val.fills=solid(C.white);\n\nNote: Text Field instance children find by name 'Quantity' — after changing characters to 'Price', findOne(n.name==='Quantity') still works by original name? Changing characters doesn't change node name. First override label1: find name 'Quantity' → set 'Quantity' (unchanged). For field2: find 'Quantity' → set 'Price'. Careful order: find before renaming. In buildTx both fields: label default 'Quantity'; field2 find 'Quantity' then set 'Price'. OK.\n\nCaptions: mkText, right-align: cap.x = 20+374-17-cap.width; cap.y = Y+25+(52-16)/2 ≈ Y+43.\n\nDialog: instance of 13:194 at (47,330), name 'Dialog'.\n\nDim: rect 414×896 black 0.55, name 'Dim', placed after all content but before dialog.\n\nWrite call E.","signature":"dad4fe6572e14ad1a8cea46e"}],"id":"8f004228-0a89-4fb2-be9e-bd205d7aff41","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1c030d6-8623-4883-b4fc-98c71a716f33","uuid":"d362a198-b1e8-4e46-b908-edf6f227ca7d","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:44:16.059Z","thinking_duration_ms":18390}
